Newsgroups: comp.unix.osf.osf1,comp.unix.programmer,comp.unix.osf.misc,comp.lang.c


Hi out there,

I am writing a program utilize the message queue (IPC) feature
in Dec Unix. 

The scenario is the queue can be created using msgget().
I use ipcs to view it. By when I call msgsnd(), it will
block there (no return) if I set the flag to 0. If I
set the flag to IPC_NOWAIT, it will return with errno = 35.
Well, somehow, the data I want to send cannot get thro.
I have check all the manual and man page. No finding.
Is the any system parameters that I need to set?

TIA.

Here's my full test code :

#include  <termio.h>
#include  <sys/types.h>
#include  <fcntl.h>
#include  <stdio.h>
#include  <sys/ipc.h>
#include  <sys/msg.h>

int   nIndexQueueId;            /* message queue id  for INDEX */

extern int   errno;      

typedef  struct {
        long    msgtype;         /* queue type           */
        char    msgbuf [ 100 ];  /* contains the data    */
} MSGQ;

MSGQ m;

void main ()
{
  int   messageid;

 m.msgtype = 1L ;
 strcpy(m.msgbuf,"This is a test msg!") ;

 if  (( messageid = msgget ((key_t)(6000L), IPC_CREAT)) == -1 ) 
       	exit (-1);
 fprintf(stderr, "[%d]", messageid);

  if ( msgsnd ( messageid, &m, strlen(m.msgbuf)+1, 0) == -1)
	fprintf(stderr, "Test Queue got problem!\n err [%d]", errno);
  else fprintf(stderr, "Test Queue OK!\n");
  printf(stderr, "[%d]\n", errno) ;

}

Regards,
Kok Fock Seng
fskok@silicon.net.my
System Administrator
Silicon Communications.



