Newsgroups: comp.sys.dec,comp.unix.osf.osf1


At my department we have one of these connected to a DEC3000-700
(currently with DU3.2d) as the main backup resource using Legato
Networker software. This device is showing some really bad habits:

1. Every 5-10 tapes there will be one or more tape(s) that will fail
to load more than, say, 1 MB. A label operation on a tape like that
will most likely fail and end up with an I/O error or just a hang in
the networker server.

2. Sometimes when (1.) happens the DAT drive will produce an I/O error
an blink _a_ _lot_ with its LEDs and will not respond to anything
short of a power cycle. 

The second problem went away last time the unit was replaced bu DEC
service. We have been using 120m DDS2 tapes from Digital, HP, Sony and
Conner and no particular type of tape stands out in this matter.

The tape loader is placed in an air-conditioned computer room with no
noticeable dust and there is a cleaning tape run every ten tapes.

It turned out that at all the other three sites at this university
that uses this autoloader (with the same software even) have more or
less experienced the same problems. The reason for bringing this up in
this group is that I'd like to find out if the problem is more
widespread than Link�ping, Sweden. So, if anybody out there has any
experience with the TLZ07L - good or bad - feel free to share that
experience.

/Erik

