I'm interested to know if anyone has figured out how to tune a kernel
to optimize packet fabrication to keep pace with OC3 speeds using
ATM interfaces.

I have an atm switch between two DEC Alpha's running OSF 4.0.  Using
classical IP, and UDP Datagrams - my throughput varies (for a given
