>Is it possible to code and configure your own file system type into DEC 
>OSF/1 3.x and DU 4.x, without needing to change the .o files for which no 
>source code is provided? 

Yes, as far as I know.

>Is there a mechanism for doing this that is officially a) supportedk
>b) documented by DEC - for example definitions of the various interface 
>functions and also kernel utilities such as buffer management.


Oh, well that's something else!  We do have third parties with their
own file system, but I don't know if they needed a source license to
figure out all the internals.  There is a source file we ship that allows
you to include a VFS dispatch table for a new FS, and the header files
describe the VFS_* macro calls to manipulate the file system and the
VOP_* calls to manipulate files.  I don't know if there's more, but if
so, it's probably less than the device driver book.

