For surveying the source program I found a workaround approach
to get the elm binaries on DU 3.2C or afterward:

Before running ./Configure, remember to make a shell escape
before Configure makes the substitution from the config.sh to
every Makefile; you could type: sh or csh to leave the Configure
temporarily to modify the config.sh.
Search the string `d_sigaction' and replace the `define' as `undef'.
It seems sigaction() existing in the libc of DU but incompatible for the
elm.

Even compiling the elmME+, I recommend to use `CC -D__STDC__' to accomplish
the compilation.

Hope this helps,
