X-Mailer: Mozilla 2.02 (Win95; I)


Quoting a Digital document:


"BLITZ TITLE: Clarification on Upgrade Installs - Digital UNIX Patches



      DEPARTMENT: Digital UNIX Problem Management    CROSS REFERENCE #'s:
                                                     (PRISM/TIME/CLD#'s)

      INTENDED AUDIENCE:  All                        PRIORITY LEVEL:  1

      (U.S./EUROPE/GIA)                              (1=TIME CRITICAL,
                                                      2=NON-TIME CRITICAL)
      =====================================================================

Subject: Clarification on Upgrade Installs and  Digital UNIX Patches

Summary:

Presently, any Digital UNIX system with patches applied that is upgraded to a
newer version of Digital UNIX via an update install may encounter subsequent
serious problems such as system crashes, hangs or other indeterminate behavior.
Such problems may be the result of conflicts between the previously applied
patches and new code loaded during the update installation.

The only way to guarantee there are no conflicts of this type is to guarantee
that no patches remain on the system before the update installation is
performed. This can be done only by (1) removing each patch that had been
applied or by (2) performing a fresh install of the current version of Digital
UNIX before the update installation. Unfortunately, no tools exist at this time
to make the task easier and less time consuming.

This information is *NOT* contained in the Installation Guide for any version
of Digital UNIX. However, plans are being made to include it in the
documentation for future versions of Digital UNIX.

Details:

Select either method 1 or 2 below.

(1) In order to perform a correct update install by first removing individual
    patches:

    a. Make a complete backup copy of everything considered valuable,

    b. Back out all of the patches applied to the current version of Digital
       version, leaving an original "clean" version of Digital UNIX,

    c. Perform the update install per the procedure in the Installation Guide
       of the new version of Digital UNIX, then

    d. Install all of the new version's patches that are available for the
       installed subsets.

(2) In order to perform a correct update install by first doing a new install
    of the current version of Digital UNIX:

    a. Make a complete backup copy of everything considered valuable,

    b. Do a total fresh install of the current version of Digital UNIX,
       following the procedures documented in the current version's
       Installation Guidllation Guide.

    c. Do the update install of the new version following the procedures
       documented in the new version's Installation Guide.

    d. Install all of the new version's patches that are available for the
       installed subsets, then

    e. Perform all of the system management activities associated with a fresh
       install, such as configuring networks, creating accounts, etc.

*********************************************************************"



