oneill@cs.uml.edu (Brian 'Doc' O'Neill) writes:

> I wouldn't call this a security hole per se, but it could result in a lot of
> resources going south...
> 
> A user informed me today that the XFree86 server has a "-query" option,
> which enabled XDMCP messages. When used in the form:
> 
> 	X -query alpha_host :1
> 
> it starts a local X server, but the user authentication is from the system
> "alpha_host" and the dtlogin program. When a user logs in, the .xsession
> file is run from alpha_host, using all alpha_host's resources, not those of
> the local Linux/*BSD box. Obviously, I don't like the idea of that...
> 
> I'm sure there is a config file somewhere to disable it, but I can't find
> any man pages related to dtlogin.
