> "Did I mention that my nose is on fire and that there are 15 badgers
>  living in my pants?" Marcus, Babylon 5

The general idea with running the X-server in query mode is to use
login and process resources on another host. In effect it makes the
computer running X merely a dumb X-terminal.

If this is not what you want, why dont you run X either just by
letting users start it with 'startx' or by running XDM on the
Linux/BSD box? If it's CDE you are after I think that Caldera (or was
it Xinside?) ships a version for Linux.

