Summary: Unix IPC FIFO library
Organization: Internet Atlanta
Keywords: IPC FIFO library
Newsgroups: comp.unix.programmer,comp.os.linux.misc,comp.unix.sys5.r4,comp.unix.osf.osf1,comp.unix.unixware.misc,alt.sources


FYI: The following source code product is available:

A very High Performance IPC library for many Unixes is available 
that delivers:

The SMQ FIFO is a library of APIs for passing fixed sized buffers, full 
duplex, between two tasks, on the same box or different boxes within a 
Cluster.  The FIFO buffer area may be SYSV shared memory or Clustered 
box memory technologies like DEC Memory Channel.  The value of this API 
is HIGH PERFORMANCE, SMP environment, FIFO delivery of buffers, low CPU 
burden, asynchronous I/O and may interface Clustered memory technologies 
like DEC Memory Channel.  

Current uses are in same box high performance IPC between Unix tasks.

To better explain what this library delivers, inferior performing but 
equivalent (same box) functionality is available from Unix SYSV message 
queues, or with alot less functionality and reliability from UDP/IP sockets.

Performance on an Intel 90Mhz P5 is 2000 pkts/sec or 8Mb/sec inter task IPC,
or on faster hardware, DEC Alpha 5/350 Mhz SMP, 18000/pkts/sec or 74Mb/sec.

The SMQ FIFO library is free for non-commercial use and more information
is available at:

http://www.compgen.com/widgets

Also avaiable are Motif widgets for: An HTML widget (very nice), Tree 
widget.  The HTML widget comes with the better part of a full Unix GUI
help sub-system.  A solution for which many commercial products are having
problems.

Cheers.

Curt Smith
curts@compgen.com




