Following is a script I've had sitting around for quite a while.
I've kinda nicknamed it 'rmsome'.  With it, I can also remove files
from, say, an entire month (rmsome Jan), or just a day (rmsome "Jan 21")
because of the -l listing on ls.  

   num=$RANDOM                                   
   ls -l | grep "$1" | cut -c55- > /tmp/kill.$num
   while read i                                  
   do                                            
        rm $i                                 
   done < /tmp/kill.$num                         
   rm /tmp/kill.$num



