XESS Enterprise Spreadsheet Adds Solaris x86 Support

CHAPEL HILL, N.C. -- February 18, 1997 --  Applied Information Systems
(AIS) announced today that it has released a version of its XESS
spreadsheet for the Solaris x86 operating system.  This version is 
completely compatible with the version for Solaris on SPARC and with the 
versions for other UNIX, OpenVMS, and Windows NT systems.

XESS is a powerful spreadsheet system for X Windows that can be used
either as a standalone application or as a widget for integration with
other applications.  As a spreadsheet, XESS includes the fullest
range of computational and graphical tools for both financial and
scientific/engineering applications.  As a development tool, XESS provides 
for the real-time integration with applications across platforms,
throughout the enterprise. 

AIS and its partners have developed a variety of applications and
options based on the XESS technology including CAD/CAM, manufacturing
automation, network management, and financial trading.  These applications 
can control all aspects of the spreadsheet and update data in real-time.

"The addition of the Solaris x86 version renews our commitment to providing
our award-winning technology on the widest range of enterprise workstations
and servers," said Arthur Coston, president of AIS.  "The Solaris x86 
version is of particular interst to clients who need to develop and deploy 
applications on a variety of workstations and high-performance servers."

With the addition of the Solaris x86 version, the XESS spreadsheet is 
now supported on:

 o Sun SPARC  -- SunOS and Solaris
 o Digital Alpha -- OpenVMS, UNIX (OSF/1), Windows NT
 o HP 9000 -- HP-UX
 o IBM RS/6000 -- AIX
 o Silicon Graphics -- IRIX
 o DEC VAX and DECstation -- OpenVMS/VMS, Ultrix
 o Data General Aviion (88/Open) -- DG/UX
 o Personal Computers (Intel) -- SCO, Solaris x86, Linux, Windows NT

XESS 3.1 is available worldwide from AIS and its partners.  AIS also
provides specialized training, support, and consulting services for XESS
and related products. 

Applied Information Systems Inc., headquartered in Chapel Hill, North
Carolina, is a 24-year-old supplier of software products and
solutions.  It specializes in multi-vendor integration applications
and advanced client/server applications. 

For more information and trial versions, see http://www.ais.com.



