An example I gave to the Operators:
Jeff Shervey - Landis & Staefa, Buffalo Grove, IL

Real-Life Example - Restore backlog.dat for Jim Brown
File was in /usr/users/brownj/data/backup.dat.
We need to position the tape to second image saveset because fullbackup1
at night first does the "/" dir followed by the "/usr" dir.
Therefore "/usr" files will be in the second image saveset on the tape.  
The tape was in the right-side drive (default tapedrive) so I didn't have
to tell it what tape device to use.

#
# cd /usr4/restore
# mt fsf 1
# vrestore -x -v -o ask /users/brownj/data/backlog.dat
vrestore: Date of the vdump save-set: Tue Jan  7 23:09:40 1997
r  ././users/
r  ././users/brownj/
r  ././users/brownj/data/
r  ././users/brownj/data/backlog.dat, 16286382
#
#

The above created a dir that looks like
/usr4/restore/usr/users/brownj/data.
The backlog.dat file was also restored here in above dir.
I then copied the backlog.dat file to Jim Brown's subdir.





