the effect of "appending" dumps the end of tapes.

The one I use for my 4mm DAT is:

dump 0bduf 63 4853070 /dev/nrmt0h /dev/device_to_backup
dump 0bduf 63 4853070 /dev/nrmt0h /dev/next_device_to_backup
...

(BTW:  b = blocking factor, d = density, u = record dump date, f =
file to use for target )

As many as will fit on a tape.  Just remember which order you placed
the dumps on the tape...

Later, to get to the files for restore, you have to position the tape
with the mt command.

i.e. to get the third dump on a tape:

mt fsf 2			(jump forward 2 files on tape)
restore -if /dev/nrmt0h

Hope this helps...

-David Taylor



