Andrew M Lau <amlau@MIT.EDU> writes:

> In Digital Unix which file must be edited so that I can su from a
> regular user account....  or is it set up to allow only certain users...
> if so which ones?
> 
> right now at the prompt if I type su I get the response:
> 
> You do not have permission to su root
> 
> Thanks for any help,
> 
> Andrew Lau
> amlau@mit.edu

To allow a user to use 'su' in Digital UNIX, that user must be a member
of the group "system".  Edit /etc/group to add that user to the "system"
group, and on the next login that user will be able to use 'su'.

