Achachila wrote:
> Sorry but I am new to Digital Unix, could anyone tell me how can I rm
> 1000 of files without getting Arg. list to long?
> I need to rm something like  *96*

Try:
   find /directory-with-your-files -name "*96*" -exec rm {} \;
This will traverse the directory tree and match and remove files
one by one, rather than trying to make one giant command line 
listing all the files.

-- 
