Kevin Oberman wrote:
> 
> "Lauer Edouard" <lauer_edi@innet.be> writes:
> 
> > The result of the ps command on the smaller window is that all caracters
> > after the end of the window width are !!!truncated!!!.
> 
> This is, unfortunately, a posix requirement. ps MUST truncate at
> terminal width to be compliant. (I didn't say it made sense, did I?)
> 
> If you can live with BSD syntax, try "ps auxww".

The alternative is to fool the system into thinking that your terminal
is wider.
You can issue a command
	stty columns 100
to tell the system that your terminal screen is 100 columns wide.  I use
emacs on
my alpha and often when I want the full output of ps I use this command
in a shell
buffer and then am able to see the full output

--
