> installation CD.  He is off looking for it, but does anybody have any 
> suggestions as to what I can do in the meantime to get the filesystems
> recreated so that I can restore from my backup tapes?
> 
> Thanks.
> 	/dwight
> 

It turns out that the situation is worse than I thought.  We borrowed a CD
from another Alpha site and I managed to rebuild my filesystems.  However,
when I went to restore from the backups, I found out that the operators
had not labeled the tapes very well (or didn't understand the incremental
backup concept), so the level 0 tape was overwritten by a later increment.
This leaves me with a patchy restore at best.

At this point I've decided to blow away the whole thing, reinstall, and
rebuild everything from scratch.  Most of the web files were developed
on another system, so we should have copies there.  It may take awhile,
but without the level 0 I don't think I have much choice.  In the future
I intend to handle the level 0 dumps myself and take the tapes home with
me.

Thanks to those who responded by email with suggestions.
	/dwight
