> I was trying to use mtool-utilities (comminication with MS-DOS floppy).
> Firstly I ran mtool 2.X (I've found it in /usr/bin/mtool). But it
> didn't work. Any of them failed with message:
> 
>         Drive 'A:' not supported
>         Cannot initialize 'A:'
> 
> Then I download mtool 3.01 and compiled and installed it successefully.
> But it doesn't work either.

I can't believe how many times I've answered this question. Can the
answer be put in a FAQ or something??!!

The answer is: Read the man page!!! 'man 5 mtools'.

This man page explains how to configure mtools for your disk drive, by
editting the file /etc/mtools.conf. My file looks like this:

drive a: file="/dev/fd0c"
        fat_bits=12
        tracks=80 heads=2 sectors=18
        nodelay

Also change the access rights to the file /dev/fd0c if you want
non-priveleged users to use the drive.

Cheers,

Matt
