Here are a few ideas: 

How are you mounting your root filesystem? With bcheckrc? Or with a fsck
then a mount -u? Because bcheckrc probably expects vold to be running to
be able to check the other filesystems, and may be upset because of
this. Or if vold is also running, then maybe LSM is upset because it
can't find the other disk.

Have you tried booting the generic kernel?

The other thing to try, of course, is to boot on the OS CD, but you
can't do that without the CD, neh?

