Sorry, I'm falling in the middle of the discussion but I have a point
to make: there is no such thing as a clock running in local time on a
Unix system.  The internal time runs in UTC, and programs outputting a
time in person-readable format are responsible for the conversion to
local time (if desired).

Summarizing: there is no problem if ntp sets your internal clock to
UTC. It's supposed to do that.

