[...]
> I was surprised to see that the values of
> MINFLOAT and MINDOUBLE
> are defined less then the compiler can work with!

Try 'cxx -ieee'.  The default compiler settings produce code that is
not IEEE conformant, since getting all the fiddly bits right creates a
lot of extra work for the processor which slows down benchmarks.  The
'-ieee' flag should fix it under 4.0--for earlier versions you need
some different set of flags, and I'm not even sure you can get the
right behavior out of cxx under older OS versions.  (Tested under DUX
4.0B with cxx 5.4-006.)
