To expand on what Allen said  ( :-) ), `man uac' to read about unaligned
accesses.  Essentially, you're accessing data that's not aligned on the proper
byte boundaries.

As Allen indicated, the best way to find out where the problems are is to
run the program under the control of a debugger (dbx and ladebug work fine
too).  From your prompt, as yourself (not root), do:

	uac p sigbus

to cause unaligned accesses to generate a bus error.  Then run your program
under control of gdb.  Gdb will catch the bus error and show you exactly where
it happened.

BTW, this is all mentioned in the FAQ for this newsgroup.

Tim
