Courtney,

I have a 3000-600, and faced the same situation.  You have to go the 2.0 
-> 3.0 -> 3.2 -> 4.0  (or something close to that) route.  Since the v2.0 
binaries will generally run under 4.0, I decived to go from a straight 
install.  Just booted from the CD and it overwrote the / and /usr 
partitions.  My additional /usr2 partition was left alone.

My main reason for this was the fear of missing something along the way.  
That's a lot of upgrades with a potential for disaster.  Plus, I think it 
save me time overall.  I ended up moving many of the programs over to 
another alpha machine and then NFS copying things back over.

Good luck!
Mike

