Ian Lintault <ian@adone.com> wrote:
>
>0 were discarded or dropped. And the number of transmits did not climb
>while I was performing >3mb ftp transfer that took about 5 minutes.
>Remeber I have a switched 100BASET to each machine.

Full duplex?  Half duplex?  What's the configuration of your network
adaptors & switches?  I'm coming into this discussion a bit late, but
the only thing I've seen that would account for such horrible
performance is having a full duplex / half duplex mis-match.

We have a number of AS500/266's connected via a 100MB full-duplex
switch.  If you set the alpha's interface into 1/2 duplex, you see
horrid performance for large xfers, and decent interactive
performance.  With the alphas & the switch in full duplex mode, we see
performance of 11104.36 KB/sec (measured via ttcp).

You might want to double check your duplex settings --look into the
'ifconfig <interface> speed [100|200]' unix commands & the 'set
'set <interface> mode [Fast|FastFD]' srm console commands.

Cheers,

Drew

