In article <32F2D81D.436F@avana.net>, jblack@avana.net wrote:

> First I would like to thank everyone who suggested solutions for using
> disklabel to
> add Seagate Barracudas to DU 3.2.  They are now online and can be
> mounted as individual
> devices through "/etc/fstab". My next question, what tool can I use to
> combine both
> 4 Gig disks into one 8 Gig virtual file system?
> 
> I don't want to mount one under the others directory structure. I want
> make them both
> act as one 8 Gig drive. I then want to have a filesystem that would
> reside across the
> two disks.

AdvFS is one approach.  With AdvFS you can join multiple disks into a
Domain.  Additional disks (or partitions) can be added or removed as
desired.

LSM is another approach.  LSM can be used to join disks into a logically
larger volume.  LSM allows joining the disks together, striping, and
mirroring of disks.

Both approaches have advantages and disadvantages from a System Managment
perspective.

