>marked as FAILED by the controller are are next to each other in the
>cabinent.

With SWXCRMGR111 should come the Storageworks utility.  The latest we have is
SWXCR122.  This provides some useful text based commands, as well as a
pretty useless gui interface.  Doesn't let you do too much with the array,
but does let you know about problems.

You should also have a floppy which can be booted from the rom prompt whichs
gives full control over the array (requires graphics console).

The utilities do allow you to put failed drives back online, however there
is no guarantee that it will fix anything.  Personally, I think these
controllers are a piece of junk.  The HSZ series are a much nicer setup,
although they do cost HEAPS more.

Good luck.

